WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.100
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.720
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.090
between Burger King in India and the US.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.833
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.190
In Burger King India, our drinks
come in one standard size,

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.470
which looks to be your small or medium,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.980
but you can also opt for a can of 330 ml.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.550
Burger King in the US, our
drinks come in four sizes.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.850
Value, small,

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.992
medium, and large.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.538
Let's measure this cup to see

00:00:30.538 --> 00:00:31.800
how much is actually in here.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.035
Does this make anybody else want to pee,

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:35.430
or is it just me?

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.660
Joe: 34 ounces.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.460
Well, it says 38 at the bottom of the cup.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.092
It ain't 38.

00:00:40.092 --> 00:00:43.133
Our Burger King fries come in two sizes,

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.965
medium and king.

00:00:45.965 --> 00:00:47.314
[angelic singing]

00:00:47.314 --> 00:00:48.990
Our fries come in four sizes.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.023
Value, small,

00:00:51.023 --> 00:00:52.765
medium, large.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.070
I remember the large
being bigger than this.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.950
I'm just glad that the fuss we rose

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.760
for the first UK-US
"Food Wars" Burger King

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.480
has resulted fry transparency.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.100
Next up, chicken fries.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.060
I didn't know this was a thing,

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.950
so I'm very excited to eat them.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.300
It should have five pieces.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.560
Three.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.790
Four.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:15.720
Five.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.100
Six!

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.573
Thank you, Burger King!

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.790
Oh, never mind.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.070
One of the fries had
broken. They gave me five.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:26.400
Ours also is one size. Nine chicken fries.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.670
It's like a pack of chicken cigarettes.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.680
Seven, eight, nine.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.000
A nice brown on brown.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.250
Yeah. We thought ahead for this one.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.455
Next one we shoot, I'm wearing all brown.

00:01:37.455 --> 00:01:38.730
I'm wearing a brown jumpsuit.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.290
We're gonna paint this brown.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.490
The most unwatchable series.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.160
Here's everything you'll find on the menu

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.070
at Burger King India that
you won't find in the US.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.710
And here's everything you
can get at a US Burger King

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.270
you can't get in India.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.820
Let's begin with the Whoppers!

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.620
This is a good time to
mention that here in India,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:59.040
most fast-food restaurants
do not serve beef or pork

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.890
to keep the religious sentiments
of both Hindus and Muslims.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.097
Conservative Hindus will not

00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:04.620
enter a restaurant that serves beef.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.958
Conservative Muslims might not

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.860
enter a restaurant that serves pork.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.330
All right. Keeping all of that in mind,

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.912
let us begin with the chicken Whopper.

00:02:11.912 --> 00:02:13.710
Whoo, boy!

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.500
OK, Burger King definitely
has larger burgers

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.480
than most other restaurants here in India.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.280
Look at this. It's the size of my face.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.603
I am the Burger King.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.080
That's so good.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.797
You might notice if you are a regular

00:02:26.797 --> 00:02:29.555
Burger King consumer of the foreign lands

00:02:29.555 --> 00:02:31.260
that if you were to eat this one,

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.790
it's a little spicier.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:33.990
And I think they've done that

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.970
because most Indians love their spice.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.290
There's a lot of bite to it.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.660
Next up, double chicken patty.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.030
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.370
This one's got some heft to it, huh?

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.410
The mutton Whopper.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.780
Mutton, if you are unaware, is goat meat,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.330
and Burger King is one of
the few fast-food chains here

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.700
that actually serves
red meat of some kind.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.960
Indians love their mutton.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.103
I love my mutton.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.120
It's definitely more meaty.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.250
Has a lot more bite to
it than the chicken.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.900
God, Burger King, what are you doing?

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.880
The quality is out of control.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.200
Every beef burger at Burger
King is a US exclusive.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.460
Got all the Whoppers.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.230
Let's start down here.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.320
The little guy, the Whopper Jr.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.490
Not enough meat, you say?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.080
You can get yourself a double Whopper.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.910
Same burger, two patties.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.830
Can they go bigger? They can.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.230
The triple Whopper.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.090
Look at this thing.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.230
Hey.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.330
Close your mouth when
you're taking a picture.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.770
The Texans of the audience

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.420
might have to help us
out in the comments here.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.040
The Texas double Whopper.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.050
Texas prides itself, from what I can tell,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.160
on always going bigger.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.290
So why wouldn't it be
the Texas triple Whopper?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.383
A rare moment where Texas was reserved.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.465
Texans of the internet,

00:03:47.465 --> 00:03:49.140
I think you guys need to step in here.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.240
I don't think that sandwich
is doing you guys proud.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.070
On to the veg options.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.140
This is a veg Whopper.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.783
I expect great things from this bad boy.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.140
I would say this is pretty lackluster.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.290
Next up, veggie double burger,

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.090
if you want double the disappointment.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.670
Another thing that we have
that technically isn't beef

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:09.990
is the Impossible Whopper,

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:12.060
which is made with Impossible beef.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.170
I'm actually very curious,

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.320
how does the Impossible
burger patty taste, Joe?

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.386
Regular beef.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.620
I have to hand it to them.
It tastes exactly the same.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.657
If you want to give the
environment a break,

00:04:24.657 --> 00:04:26.100
maybe get one of these
every once in a while.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.810
Next up, we have an exclusive
King collection of burgers.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:34.890
These better be quite
royal and aristocratic.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:38.310
No. 1, Hot 'n' Cheezy veg.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.623
Lot of jalapeños.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.970
The patty actually has,
like, cheese melt in it.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.500
Hot 'n' Cheezy Kings collection,

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.730
on a scale of common
villager to the king himself,

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.400
I would rate this village bard.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.233
Once in a while

00:04:54.233 --> 00:04:56.850
you want him there just
to appease a few people,

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.850
but otherwise pretty lackluster.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.100
Paneer Royale.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.710
Just by the name itself,

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.320
this one should be incredible.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.050
So, paneer, if you don't
know, is cottage cheese,

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.720
and here in India, it is almost a staple.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.400
We eat it in everything.
We eat it in curries.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.680
We sometimes just sear
it and eat it plain.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.113
And obviously it had to
make its way to burgers.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.960
The paneer is really
good. Chewy and delicious.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.930
I would rate the Paneer Royale

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.280
a local baron.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.230
Helps the king around a little bit.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.680
Now on to the two non-veg
options. We have fiery chicken.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.150
Plain and simple.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.433
They just want this meat to blow my mind.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.850
It's just spicy. That's all it is.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.590
It doesn't have the depth of flavor

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.180
that the chicken Whoppers did.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.013
Chicken tandoori.

00:05:46.013 --> 00:05:47.730
If you guys don't know what a tandoor is,

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.670
it's basically this cylindrical oven

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:54.090
that we heat up using wood fire
and charcoal traditionally,

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:58.110
and we use it to create
everything from kebabs to breads.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.820
I doubt all Burger King outlets

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.650
have an actual tandoor
in their restaurants,

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.880
but let's see if they were able

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.653
to replicate that smoky flavor.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:11.070
On a scale of absolute
street urchins to maharajas,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.460
I would rate these two court traitors

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:17.700
that tried to backstab the
king, and now they're on trial.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.520
They have a lot of bark
but not enough bite.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.170
They're gonna be executed.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:24.690
Non-Whopper burgers, aka burgers.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.545
You can get yourself
something called the Big King.

00:06:26.545 --> 00:06:28.260
And that's what it looks
like. Don't have it.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:31.950
What we do have is the
single quarter-pound King.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.540
Bacon King!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.363
I would say generous amount of bacon.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:37.403
It's great.

00:06:37.403 --> 00:06:39.990
Then these little, much more
reasonable-size burgers.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:40.950
Bacon cheeseburger.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.253
Bacon double cheeseburger.

00:06:42.253 --> 00:06:44.520
A bacon-free double cheeseburger, right?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.920
One of the most hilarious
things on the Burger King menu

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.097
is, of course, the Rodeo burger,

00:06:48.097 --> 00:06:50.190
a burger with barbecue
sauce and onion rings,

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.600
because why not?

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:52.620
Then you got cheeseburger.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.600
Regular dry-ass hamburger.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:55.620
Who cares?

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.030
Enough kingly sandwiches.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:58.435
It's now time for the regular

00:06:58.435 --> 00:07:00.480
vegetarian options that they have.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.430
We have crispy veg.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.480
Crispy veg double.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.430
Crispy veg with cheese.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.690
BK classic.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.610
BK classic with cheese.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.530
Lite Whopper Jr.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.020
And Lite Whopper Jr. with cheese.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.840
Why is it called Lite Whopper Jr.?

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.180
How many more things do
you need to add to the name

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.530
to make it seem small?

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:24.450
Mini lite small Whopper
junior kindergartner burger.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.490
How about that next time, Burger King?

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.243
OK, I don't want to try
any more veg burgers,

00:07:28.243 --> 00:07:31.290
but this one, the BK classic
veg, seems different.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.270
Like, the bun looks to be the same,

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:36.870
but they've definitely
used more perky buns here.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.933
Don't use that audio clip out of context.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.320
OK. Finally.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.610
If you're a vegetarian,

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.450
I would recommend the
BK classic with cheese.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.320
Boom.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.180
Although it is currently
for a limited time,

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.740
I thought I would share with
you guys, here in the US,

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:56.790
we have the Southwest
options at Burger King,

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:59.730
starting with the Southwest bacon Jr.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:00.990
Southwest Whopper.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.970
The Southwest Impossible Whopper.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.560
What makes a Southwest?

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.930
Ooh, I'm seeing, like,
crispy little chippy guys.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.610
Ooh, spicy. Ooh, it's got some heat to it.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.660
Yeah, there's guacamole on here. Hang on.

00:08:12.406 --> 00:08:13.800
I kinda fuck with it.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.500
I wouldn't eat if I didn't
work at "Food Wars," you know?

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.450
And now for the chicken sandwiches.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.510
These look so tiny
compared to the Whoppers.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.730
We have crispy chicken.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.050
Crispy chicken double.

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.910
Crispy chicken with cheese.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.560
BK classic chicken.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.840
Spicy grill chicken.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.960
Big smoky grill chicken.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.780
Lite Whopper chicken Jr.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.356
Lite Whopper double chicken Jr.

00:08:38.356 --> 00:08:42.393
And Lite Whopper chicken Jr. with cheese.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.320
Yes! I could work at
Burger King right now.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:47.970
We're going to try just
two of these burgers

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.650
just to see if they're any different.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:53.253
First one, the spicy grill chicken.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.530
Oh, my God.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.170
I can imagine myself
going to a drive-through,

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.912
taking one of these, driving to work,

00:08:59.912 --> 00:09:01.710
sitting in Silk Board traffic,

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:04.050
getting annoyed with all
the other people honking,

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.060
realizing I should have
gotten a bigger burger,

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.430
and next day, ordering two. Nice.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:12.663
Next up, the big smoky grill chicken.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.440
I don't see how this is smoky at all.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.260
In fact, it's kind of sweet.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:22.170
On to the non-beef options.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.090
I personally think these
new Ch'King sandwiches

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.200
are fantastic.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.850
The Ch'King,

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.970
that's C-H-apostrophe-King,
because it's Burger King.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:32.502
Spicy Ch'King sandwich. Same thing.

00:09:32.502 --> 00:09:34.620
Got some spicy sauce on
it. This is very good.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.780
If you like these but
want a little more veggies

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.790
because you're some old fogy,

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.350
here you go, vegetables.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.970
They also make the Ch'King deluxe.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.710
Deluxe equals lettuce and tomato.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:47.730
This car crash of a
sandwich is the spicy ...

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.250
actually, the spicy with veggies
is actually kind of nice.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.720
The coolness of the lettuce

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.350
and the tomato actually
counterbalances the spice.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:57.750
The original chicken sandwich,

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:00.270
shaped like the new iPhone
for some strange reason.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:01.350
This guy's been around forever.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.520
It's their answer to the McChicken.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.200
It tastes exactly like a McChicken.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.298
Chicken Jr. Look at this little guy.

00:10:06.298 --> 00:10:07.920
A spicy chicken Jr.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:11.580
And last, the only non-chicken
thing in the chicken section

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.170
is the big fish.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.380
And now for a set of snacks

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.773
that comes under their Stunner menu.

00:10:17.982 --> 00:10:20.460
[whistling]

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:23.040
We have King egg burger.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.570
King egg wrap.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:26.222
Crispy veg wrap.

00:10:26.222 --> 00:10:28.500
Veg crunchy volcano.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.646
That's right. This is not even a wrap.

00:10:30.646 --> 00:10:33.540
This is a little geological formation.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.070
Tikki Twist burger.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.510
Veg makhani burger.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.790
And chicken makhani burger.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.410
And finally, crispy chicken wrap

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.050
and crunch chicken volcano.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.520
All right, the first burger we're trying

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.605
is the chicken makhani burger.

00:10:46.605 --> 00:10:49.320
So, makhan means butter,

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.450
and it also means a lot to us Indians.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.610
You just walk into a room
and you say "makhan,"

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:54.930
it will resound through the room.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.670
Like, people's eyes will perk up.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.863
The hairs on their arms will rise.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:03.126
Oh, my God, yeah ... mm.

00:11:03.126 --> 00:11:04.518
OK, so they've gone for, like,

00:11:04.518 --> 00:11:07.620
a butter chicken, more makhani flavor,

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.870
but it just tastes like tomato puree

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.330
over a stale chicken patty.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:16.950
Next thing that I really want
to try is the volcano itself.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.750
And I think this is their answer
to Taco Bell's Crunchwrap.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.550
Oh, that's pretty good.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.070
You were this close to
offending two communities

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:28.680
and Mother Earth herself, but pretty good.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.530
Next thing I'm going to
try is an Aloo Tikki Twist.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:32.970
Tikki Twist sounds like a cocktail,

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:35.430
but aloo tikki is actually,

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:38.400
it's like mashed potato
fried with breadcrumbs,

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.660
and it's used in chaats.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.340
It's used in a lot of other dishes.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:46.020
And they put these crispy
shards of what seems to be

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:49.425
the same material in the volcano!

00:11:49.425 --> 00:11:50.640
["The X-Files" music]

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.528
Illuminati confirmed.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:57.246
On to breakfasts!

00:11:57.246 --> 00:11:59.910
We got breakfast at the BK in the US.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.280
You can get an assortment
of Croissan'wiches,

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.005
biscuits, melts.

00:12:04.005 --> 00:12:05.255
I didn't get all of them.

00:12:05.255 --> 00:12:06.210
Starting down here.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:08.160
A Croissan'wich, of course, for
those of you not in America,

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:12.660
is they took a croissant
and stuffed eggs and cheese

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.130
and your choice of breakfast meat.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.720
Bacon, egg, and cheese croissant.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:17.310
Sausage, egg, and cheese croissant.

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:19.440
Ham, egg, and cheese croissant.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.970
Bacon, egg, and cheese biscuit.

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.650
Sausage, egg, and cheese biscuit.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.270
Ham, egg, and cheese biscuit.

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:25.920
Cheesy ham breakfast melt.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.630
Sausage and cheese breakfast melt.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:29.490
Cheesy bacon breakfast melt.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:32.340
And for both the Croissan'wiches
and the biscuits,

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:35.130
you can also get pretty
much every combination

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:39.362
of meat, egg, and cheese on
said biscuit or Croissan'wich.

00:12:39.362 --> 00:12:40.890
Egg-normous burrito.

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:41.970
Ah, no, no, no, no, no.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:44.400
I am not starting off my morning
with this. No, thank you.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.560
This looks like a dirty diaper.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.090
Like, what is any of this?

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:49.581
I feel like if I bit this,

00:12:49.581 --> 00:12:51.389
like, one bite of this in the morning,

00:12:51.389 --> 00:12:52.620
and I'm on the toilet.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.300
Get yourself two platters.

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.100
Sausage and pancakes platter.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.230
And this one, I think, is,
like, the platter deluxe.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.400
You get yourself pancakes,

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:00.420
get yourself bacon,

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.440
get yourself eggs,

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.880
and, of course, syrup.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.830
Next up, chicken wings.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.350
Burger King here sells
boneless chicken wings.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.900
They feel like chicken tenders.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.940
They're super meaty.
It's like proper chicken.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:14.385
It's not like that processed, nuggety

00:13:14.385 --> 00:13:16.770
chicken-juice thing that happens.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.410
In the US, our Burger King has nuggets,

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:23.850
and they come in four
pieces and eight pieces.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:28.260
I asked the Burger King
employees about the 16-piece,

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.720
and they said they don't have a 16-piece.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.000
They just give you two eight-pieces.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.270
Now it's time for Burger
King India sides and sauces.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.760
No. 1, we have the
classic peri-peri fries.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.380
They give it to you with a little sachet

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.350
of the peri-peri powder
and a little shake bag.

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:44.767
Pour it in there.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:51.620
Voilà! Your simple plain
fries are now peri-peried.

00:13:51.916 --> 00:13:53.257
Hm.

00:13:53.257 --> 00:13:55.170
Go with McDonald's peri-peri fries.

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:56.430
I'm sorry, Burger King.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:58.140
Too powdery. Almost chalky.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.994
And the flavor is not quite there.

00:13:59.994 --> 00:14:01.410
[coughs]

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:02.243
OK.

00:14:04.257 --> 00:14:06.180
Peri-peri fries has come
back with a vengeance.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.340
Fair enough. There is
a bit of spice to it.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:11.100
Next up, cheesy fries.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.050
Italian cheesy fries.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.150
And I don't know what makes these Italian,

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:17.910
but I think it's a whole lot of oregano.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:20.610
And finally, veggie strips.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:22.418
Well, at the BK here in the US,

00:14:22.418 --> 00:14:24.360
you can get yourself onion rings.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.708
Jalapeño cheddar bites.

00:14:26.708 --> 00:14:28.020
See what one of these looks like.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.100
Mozzarella stick.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.170
Mott's applesauce.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.140
Can't have nuggets without sauces!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.800
You know what that means!

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.360
Sauce talk.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.060
As for the dips, we have Easy Cheesy.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.710
Twisted mustard.

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.630
Fiery Hell.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:50.190
They literally named one
of their dips Fiery Hell.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.170
First up, Buffalo sauce.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:53.871
Honey mustard. Ranch.

00:14:53.871 --> 00:14:55.110
Sweet and sour.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:56.580
Zesty sauce?

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.780
Do we know what this is?

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.530
That is just mayonnaise
and, like, brown mustard.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:02.820
Marinara sauce.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:04.980
Salsa del Sol.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.450
It is milkshake time.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.670
Burger King has three flavors right now.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:13.110
They have mango, berry
blast, and chocolate.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:14.760
Guys, at the time of filming this,

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.820
it is currently mango
season here in India.

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:20.400
None of you have tasted a real mango

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.070
until you've tasted the king
of all mangoes, Alphonso,

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.450
available here.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.500
Everywhere you go right now,

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.780
you're going to get a
delicious mango milkshake.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.550
We also make something called aamras,

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:33.090
which is like a delicious mango juice

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:34.710
that we eat with puris and stuff.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.823
Let's see if this compares
to fresh mango juice.

00:15:40.362 --> 00:15:42.660
Oh, it's pretty good.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.070
It's not too sweet.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:48.420
It does kind of taste like
mango ice cream sort of mixed.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.370
But I like it. I really like it.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.750
Next up, berry blast.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.460
Paper straws. Burger King, thank you.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:55.863
The dolphins appreciate
it just as much as I do.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:01.320
Whoa, I did not expect that flavor.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:04.470
Here, we have something
called black currant ice cream

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:08.190
that's rampant in very demented families

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.800
that order the black currant ice cream.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.200
I'm sorry to single out these
Indian families like this,

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.850
but this tastes like that.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:16.080
I'm sensing a pattern here.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.030
So it won't be a surprise to me

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.800
if the chocolate milkshake

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:23.820
also just tastes like
watered-down chocolate ice cream.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.580
The mango one, I suppose
if it wasn't mango season,

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.470
you could go and get a mango milkshake,

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:30.960
but otherwise, go to any other fruit

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.610
or milkshake store in India,

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:35.880
get a nice thick mango
shake with actual mangoes.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:36.930
Way better.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.360
On to the cold drinks.
Let's start with the shakes.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:41.160
Over here, we have a frozen Coke.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.230
You can also get a
frozen Fanta wild cherry.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.810
Sounds amazing. Our Burger
King did not have it.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.273
First one is this, the Oreo shake.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.190
Why is that so good?

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:53.670
It's like a shake made out
of the stuff in the middle.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:54.510
Brilliant idea.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.823
And you can also get chocolate Oreo shake.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.490
No, it's not. This one's better.
But this one's very good.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:00.780
Desserts!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:01.950
I'm a sucker for desserts,

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:05.130
but why would you order
dessert from a fast-food place?

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.530
Unless I'm going to be proven wrong.

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:11.310
First up, they have chocolate mousse cup.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.800
OK, it's got a little bit
of cake at the bottom.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.870
Chocolate, chocolate,
chocolate at the top.

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:17.223
Chocolate chips on the top.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.250
Too decadent. Very sweet.

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:22.590
Next up, they have a choco lava cup,

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:26.850
keeping in theme with their
random volcano-based food items.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.220
And I'm sure this would
ooze out chocolate,

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:31.137
but you have to heat it first.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.820
That is so sweet!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.315
When would I eat this?
I'm trying to think of

00:17:37.315 --> 00:17:39.630
when I would eat something this sweet.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:40.463
Never.

00:17:40.463 --> 00:17:41.730
We have three dessert exclusives.

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.400
The first one is this,
the Hershey's sundae pie.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.750
Chocolate chip cookies.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.550
A soft-serve cup or cone.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:48.420
Where is it, Joe?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.690
Well, it's roughly 100 degrees
here in Southern California,

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.340
and that thing would've melted into a soup

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.990
before we even got it to the studio.

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:58.110
Imagine either a
soft-serve ice cream cone,

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.720
or a melted soft-serve ice cream cone

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.160
would be more accurate.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.940
As for cold drinks, we
have Pepsi; Mountain Dew;

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.880
Mirinda, which is an orange soda;

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.590
and iced tea.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.890
All of these are under the
PepsiCo range of products.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:15.780
And, of course, in India,

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:18.630
the Pepsi slogan is,
"Har Ghoont Mein Swag,"

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.842
which means, "Every
sip has a lot of swag."

00:18:21.842 --> 00:18:23.490
And I have to live with this cringe

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:25.110
for the rest of my life now.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:26.430
Here in the US,

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:29.490
we have obviously a
variety of exclusive drinks

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:31.200
you can't get in India.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.130
Coke.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.330
Dr. Pepper.

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:34.440
Diet Coke.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:35.640
There it is. Barq's, baby.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:36.510
Fanta orange.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.550
I should say that at
least the BKs that I go to

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.500
here in sunny Southern California

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:42.420
has those Coke Freestyle machines, so.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.310
You can also get yourself an orange juice.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:46.560
It's really funny looking at orange juice

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:47.940
next to orange drink.

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.290
Like, look at the difference with it.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:51.000
Orange juice. Orange drink.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.770
Capri Sun apple juice.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.150
Burger King iced coffee.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.258
The BK café, which is, of course, coffee.

00:18:56.258 --> 00:18:57.091
Milk.

00:18:58.140 --> 00:18:59.820
Let's talk price.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:04.350
A single Indian chicken Whopper
will cost you 199 rupees,

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:08.190
or 1.56 US dollars at
current conversion rates.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:11.580
In the US, a Whopper costs $8.79,

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:14.910
or 668 Indian rupee.

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:18.990
That's around a 236% increase in price.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:21.840
Make it a meal with medium
fries and a large drink,

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:26.670
and it'll cost you 383
rupees, or 5.03 US dollars.

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:28.920
Add a medium fry and a
medium drink to the order,

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:32.478
and that brings the price to $16.37,

00:19:32.478 --> 00:19:35.744
or 1,246 Indian rupee.

00:19:35.744 --> 00:19:39.330
Again, about a 225% increase.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:40.590
Now upgrade to the large size,

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:44.460
and it's 407 rupees, or 5.35 US dollars.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:47.526
Make it a large, $16.77,

00:19:47.526 --> 00:19:50.851
or 1,276 Indian rupee.

00:19:50.851 --> 00:19:53.425
That's a 214% increase.

00:19:53.425 --> 00:19:57.000
200 rupees for a single burger
is actually very expensive.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.241
And while fast food in the US

00:19:59.241 --> 00:20:01.524
and other foreign countries
might seem like something

00:20:01.524 --> 00:20:04.080
that the average person can easily afford,

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:06.120
here in India, this is expensive,

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.770
and only the upper-middle
class and the rich

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.870
can actually go out and
have a burger like this.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.390
In fact, in Mumbai, where
we're filming this right now,

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.580
our most popular street food is vada pav,

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.890
which is like a potato burger,

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:20.190
and it costs just 15
rupees, which is $0.20.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.720
It can fill you up.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.480
Downgrade the cost. Upgrade the taste.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.980
Get a vada pav.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.480
To better illustrate the price difference,

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:30.000
let's compare the US large Whopper combo

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.640
to our combination of two Whoppers,

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.440
two crispy chicken sandwiches,

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:38.610
five-piece chicken strips,
king fries, and four drinks.

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.890
All of this still costs less,

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.264
at just 1,102 rupees,

00:20:43.264 --> 00:20:46.631
or 14.45 US dollars.

00:20:46.631 --> 00:20:48.330
We would have to add a
crispy veg with cheese

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.530
and a crispy chicken with cheese

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:51.810
to get around the same price.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.300
But again, I have to
remind you that in $14,

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:55.710
an average family here in India

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.783
could eat at home for a week.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.210
Calories time.

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:02.875
My favorite part of these
videos because I realize

00:21:02.875 --> 00:21:06.510
how much I should not be eating this food.

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:08.640
Let's start off with a
crispy chicken sandwich

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:10.080
from Burger King.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.290
Ahem. It has 430 calories.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:14.123
And in the US,

00:21:14.123 --> 00:21:18.120
our crispy chicken
sandwich is 670 calories.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.711
Next up is one of Burger King India's

00:21:19.711 --> 00:21:22.694
most popular burgers, the veg Whopper,

00:21:22.694 --> 00:21:25.544
at 728 calories.

00:21:25.544 --> 00:21:29.010
Imagine that. High calories, low taste.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.480
We don't have that, but in the US,

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:33.090
our Burger King does have
the Impossible Whopper,

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:35.790
which contains 630 calories.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:37.320
Next, let's compare the fries.

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:39.840
An average box of king-sized fries

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.930
will cost you 535 calories.

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:44.940
If I had to choose between these fries

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.680
and an hour of cycling,

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:48.540
that's very, like,
probably skip the cycling.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:51.690
But this is still bad.
It's a lot of calories.

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:55.590
And in the US, a large
fry has 430 calories.

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:56.910
And now, for some reason

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:59.550
if you're really looking
to pack on those calories,

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:03.630
introducing Burger King India's
most calorific sandwich,

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:07.163
the masala veg Whopper,

00:22:07.163 --> 00:22:12.163
at a total of 734 calories.

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:13.410
Damn!

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.540
The website of Burger King India also says

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:18.210
they sell a 15-piece
grilled chicken wings,

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:21.480
with a total of 1,256 calories.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.970
But we called a bunch of
stores, it was unavailable,

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:25.620
and I think they discontinued it

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:28.200
because they did not want
to kill half the country.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:30.270
Oh, yo!

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:31.380
Yeah.

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:34.260
This is definitely a block of calories.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:35.190
And in the US BK,

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:39.120
our most calorific sandwich
is this, the Bacon King.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:44.112
Just one of these bad
boys, 1,359 calories.

00:22:44.112 --> 00:22:45.653
Oof!

00:22:45.653 --> 00:22:46.650
God dammit.

00:22:46.650 --> 00:22:49.292
Brown on brown on brown.
Brown on brown on brown!

00:22:49.292 --> 00:22:52.260
Brown, brown, brown, brown, brown.

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:53.940
Hey, you got to hand it to
these fast-food companies, man.

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:55.410
They make this shit look real appetizing

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:56.580
for what is literally

00:22:56.580 --> 00:22:58.330
how many different shades of brown?

